cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software and data package, please cite this versioned release and the associated article."
title: "rk-choi-complete-positivity: complete-positivity regions of Runge-Kutta discretizations of phase-covariant qubit dynamics (code and data)"
type: software
version: 4.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-18
license: MIT
url: "https://github.com/Weyl-Center-for-Mathematical-Physics/rk-choi-complete-positivity/releases/tag/v4.0.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Weyl-Center-for-Mathematical-Physics/rk-choi-complete-positivity"
abstract: >-
  Exact symbolic calculations, certified root brackets, an independent
  first-principles verifier of the article's claims, the Richardson-extrapolation
  corollary of the signed first-defect law, candidate-map tests, pointwise
  transverse-field certificates, certified adaptive-guard telemetry, deterministic
  figures and tables with accessibility audits, and regression tests supporting
  finite-step complete-positivity classifications of Runge-Kutta discretizations
  of phase-covariant qubit Lindblad dynamics. The current tree is in bit/; the
  root src/, data/, figures/ and supplement/ directories preserve the earlier
  zero-precession release v1.0.0 unchanged.
